<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nanyue</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/204-bce">204</a>–111 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Nam Việt, Southern Yue, Triệu dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nanyue was an ancient kingdom in what is now southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, founded in 204 BCE by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhao-tuo">Zhao Tuo</a>, with its capital at Panyu. It covered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangdong">Guangdong</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangxi">Guangxi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hainan">Hainan</a> and central to northern Vietnam. Its rulers called themselves emperors while paying the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> only symbolic obeisance, and they brought Chinese-style administration and writing to the south while encouraging the mixing of Yue and Han cultures. When the king Zhao Xing sought union with the Han in 113 BCE, his prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lu-jia">Lü Jia</a> killed him, and in 111 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu of Han</a> sent 100,000 troops and ended the kingdom. The name Vietnam derives from Nam Việt.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Han armies also expanded southward, conquering <b>Nanyue</b> in 111 BCE, northeast into Korea in 108 BCE, and westward into Central Asia as far as the Ferghana Valley, outflanking the Xiongnu by securing allied states along their western flank.</blockquote><a href="/empire/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The name Viet Nam was granted by the Qing emperor Jiaqing in 1804, after Gia Long asked for Nam Viet, which recalled the ancient kingdom of <b>Nanyue</b> in southern China.</blockquote><a href="/empire/nguyen-dynasty">Nguyen dynasty · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
